# Build correctness: keep host-generated BUILD CACHES out of the Docker build context.
#
# Root cause this fixes: with no .dockerignore, `COPY . .` (apps/yelli/Dockerfile)
# pulled the host's apps/yelli/.next — including the incremental .next/cache — into
# the builder. `next build` then reused that STALE cache and emitted a standalone
# bundle containing an outdated compiled @yelli/db / Prisma client input shape, even
# though the on-disk client was freshly regenerated. Symptom: LAN-admin invitation
# create failed with `Argument 'tenant' is missing` despite the nullable-FK migration
# being applied and the code being correct. Excluding .next forces a clean build.
#
# NOTE: node_modules is intentionally NOT excluded — the current Dockerfile only
# copies root + apps/yelli node_modules from the deps stage and depends on `COPY . .`
# to supply packages/*/node_modules (e.g. the prisma CLI in packages/db). Excluding
# node_modules breaks `prisma generate` in the builder. A cleaner long-term fix is to
# install all workspace deps inside the builder; left as a follow-up to avoid
# destabilizing the build here.

# Next.js build output + incremental cache (regenerated by `next build`)
.next
**/.next
out
**/out

# Turbo / tooling build caches
.turbo
**/.turbo

# VCS metadata
.git

# Logs / coverage
coverage
**/coverage
*.log
npm-debug.log*
